<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d11a3ce61737cd4c73b0db8ef44fb0b550ca0db5313287c7908a8d82ad586a2</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany is shaken by an espionage and treason scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:585e85e76e014bd20bad0f9f243b006ee135be456291a4b04e7dada5affd3142</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-shaken-by-an-espionage-and-treason-scandal/a-79566578--54ee39e5baab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-shaken-by-an-espionage-and-treason-scandal/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e04c722dfebe0e623bd81701c98555239eea94bafb1504476c73a5b7c38154bc</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain court lifts Puigdemont arrest warrant, clearing way for his return home ahead of November elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34eee1a3c29990fb006c464fd2296b7936f3410c509df282f72b0ea134b7358a</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elect/a-79565853--7635b4e28c09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elections/a-79565853?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Catalan separatist leader Carles Puigdemont fled Spain in 2017 after launching an independence bid. The court's decision means he can return home without fear of arrest after almost a decade in exile.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As more Iranian women reject hijab rules, regime looks at new ways to force compliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c68c9048ffd6eac713dcaf7656f52af929559250eaf071dd2fd2f2433473bb12</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962--9c09f80416a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As more women in Iran reject rules on wearing hijab headscarves, hardliners are shifting focus from "morality police" street enforcement towards social pressure in workplaces, services and businesses.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Southeast Asia's haze crisis: Have lessons been learned?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12d29bc022d2e19276c92ca966f31765c255884ffccdd903900871fdf0da542b</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992--f0834d091bdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven years after catastrophic fires prompted promises of tougher action, Southeast Asia is again choking on transboundary haze, raising questions about whether the region has learned the lessons of 2015.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray war may spill over to Eritrea — helped by Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's rhetoric</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7a5e1a0e9468cea713e330075ddceec8a4824387a88ba67bd8666c889ed79bb</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957--f357fb8ada5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed is consolidating power, but he must contend with a regional alliance opposing him and a Tigray conflict that could spill over into Eritrea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ee49fe54d2f099b4b1d6dc733cd0c431f31e6520a70781072b9f844fbc024de</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Literature Prize: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4d72d768c69b4e7a399c2b26556909b9aa3e78b4a68e93809143a2b1a998bea</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--42983d639d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in Literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Spain approves new emergency housing measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44d8f1143a6b37193add61de846059d34c43da303cb6589b86dc7a641f8e8720</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-approves-new-emergency-housing-measures/a-79564344--ba63f57648f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-approves-new-emergency-housing-measures/a-79564344?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Spanish government has approved a pair of emergency housing decrees, including extended eviction protections and limits on property speculation, after major protests rocked Barcelona.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian military plane crash kills all 25 on board</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4de91f233cc4bdb9030019085af6454191741f73cd5d7d7d061d898f0adbe</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigerian-military-plane-crash-kills-all-25-on-board/a-79552403--b7b9eaace4c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigerian-military-plane-crash-kills-all-25-on-board/a-79552403?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams searched the crash site after the military aircraft went down in southern Nigeria, with everyone on board now confirmed to have died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db4b07a994c18998f449bb9939c47e507e438e8c8c1c2f834235bf5b948aa39e</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death/a-79563120--66be6cae64d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death/a-79563120?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The patient arrived in Kenya over the weekend from the Democratic Republic of Congo before testing positive for the virus. Health authorities are on high alert and monitoring for more cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading claims spark plague fears in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1337da7eee6a59024ecd47b62467b8bfde5047d8b7d14cc561846c29837fca89</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752--eaca60a52c9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of a lab worker at a plague research institute in Russia has sparked claims about a lab accident, hundreds of infections and international spread. Some of these viral narratives are misleading.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AI models keep hacking real systems during tests. What does this mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a57757fb0fcae2227df2ed20a5f952703b4ee85638142ab202dc0bd30a36fa31</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943--07f5722af213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI models have repeatedly broken into real commercial and government systems during safety tests during 2026. Cybersecurity researcher Thorsten Holz explains what that means, and why he isn't expecting a robot uprising.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Physics Prize goes to Francis Halzen for neutrino work</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3611c1aded41ccd7f491d52283e6d1ecfc6cd64869ddc38a7327178eabeaaeea</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-physics-prize-goes-to-francis-halzen-for-neutrino-work/a-79561506--0abe3a1da6b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-physics-prize-goes-to-francis-halzen-for-neutrino-work/a-79561506?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Halzen got the Nobel for his contributions to the IceCube neutrino Observatory and discovery of high-energy neutrinos, described as "ghostly messengers from space."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces a triple threat from Russia, China and domestic far-right extremists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0868a4c4b41436558707682afa673291bdd085e2261a35da728ebb586f863605</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490--8059184d93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a rare public hearing Germany's intelligence agencies identified Russia as the country's most dangerous adversary. The threat from China is also coming into focus. And the homegrown far right also poses a challenge.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>France: Trade unions join students in major demonstration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f37227cd48c48e22ff5306a0e970c7b295ff49eb5186261d0ce0eec4ba79172b</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-trade-unions-join-students-in-major-demonstration/a-79560273--719efa3885e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-trade-unions-join-students-in-major-demonstration/a-79560273?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people took to the streets at nationwide protests against poor learning conditions for students in France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's ex-spy chief arrested for espionage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a57960c3cd2b5278a111359eba7c5d165dd278b4aa75dd8d81f9644cfb2bc12</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278--e631ff19ef7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning, the man who once led Germany's spy service, is now under investigation for passing on state secrets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Quebec separatists return to power, promise new independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7dd5cc109ce0567f90147cf73839e6dc4c72bd8f16f1bd5f8bcd185ac4d1d69</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-quebec-separatists-return-to-power-promise-new-independence-referendum/a-79558642--c145b9836641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-quebec-separatists-return-to-power-pro